    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Network domains",
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### 5G SA Roaming \u2014 domain map\n\n| | **VISITED (VPLMN)** | **HOME (HPLMN)** | **IPX** | **RAN** |\n|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| NF | vAMF \u00b7 vSMF \u00b7 vUPF | AUSF \u00b7 UDM \u00b7 UDR \u00b7 PCF | SBI proxy | gNB \u00b7 UE |\n| Color | `#1565C0` blue | `#2E7D32` green | `#EF6C00` orange | `#6A1B9A` purple |\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Signalling call-flow (open beside Grafana)",
      "id": 2,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Live sequence diagram\n\n**[Open call-flow ladder in new tab \u2197](http://127.0.0.1:8010/static/roaming-callflow.html?api=http://127.0.0.1:8010/ladder/latest)**\n\n- Auto-refreshes every 10s from `flow-exporter /ladder/latest`\n- **Step status (arrow border):** green = **observed** \u00b7 yellow = **partial_expected** \u00b7 red = **missing**\n- **Message role colors (when wired on Ubuntu):** \ud83d\udd34 red = **request** \u00b7 \ud83d\udfe2 green = **success response** \u00b7 \ud83d\udfe0 orange = **intermediate/policy** (PCF/NRF hops)\n- **B1 same-PLMN 001/01** \u00b7 **No SEPP/N32** \u00b7 TC-05 LBO MEASURED\n\n> Grafana cannot embed iframes safely \u2014 use the link above for the full Auth \u2192 Reg \u2192 PDU ladder.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Signalling steps (Auth \u2192 Reg \u2192 PDU)",
      "id": 230,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 14,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "roaming_flow_step_total > 0",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "labelsToFields",
          "options": {
            "mode": "columns"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "Value": true,
              "__name__": true,
              "instance": true,
              "job": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "phase": "Phase",
              "step": "Step",
              "procedure": "Signalling message",
              "result": "Status"
            },
            "indexByName": {
              "Phase": 0,
              "Step": 1,
              "Signalling message": 2,
              "Status": 3
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "fields": {},
            "sort": [
              {
                "field": "Step"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "filterable": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Status"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "color-background",
                  "mode": "basic"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "observed": {
                        "text": "OBSERVED",
                        "color": "#43A047"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "partial_expected": {
                        "text": "PARTIAL",
                        "color": "#FBC02D"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "missing": {
                        "text": "MISSING",
                        "color": "#E53935"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Fault domain attribution",
      "id": 3,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Fault domain attribution\n\nUse multi-point capture evidence before assigning blame. Implementation: `harness/trace-validation/fault_domain.py`.\n\n| Domain | When to attribute |\n|--------|-------------------|\n| **HOME** | Cause or failure response originates from HSS/UDM/AUSF/UDR (e.g. 5xx SBI from home NF, Diameter answer from HSS) |\n| **VISITED** | Local AMF/MME rejects before home is reached; attach succeeds through auth but fails in visited PDU path |\n| **IPX** | No response within Diameter/HTTP2 timer window, or transport failure at DRA/SBI proxy hop \u2014 **not SEPP/N32 (absent V14)** |\n| **RAN/UE** | Failure before NAS reaches core (RRC/NGAP/S1AP establishment) |\n| **NTN impairment** | Same cause codes as above but time-correlated with active netem profile on ran-net \u2014 UNVERIFIED timer correlation until measured |\n\n**Cause code references (definitions only \u2014 lab must trace MEASURED codes):**\n- 5GMM causes: 3GPP TS 24.501 Annex A \u2014 UNVERIFIED against live pcaps until TC run\n- EMM causes: 3GPP TS 24.301 Annex A \u2014 DEFERRED (no LTE MME)\n- Diameter Experimental-Result: TS 29.272 \u00a77.3 \u2014 see verification-register V1/V2\n- HTTP problem details: TS 29.500 \u00a75.2.7 \u2014 UNVERIFIED until SBI error pcaps parsed\n\n> **INDETERMINATE** when evidence is insufficient \u2014 never guess."
      }
    },
